curl -I https://example.com
curl -v https://example.com
curl http://localhost:3000
wget https://example.com/file.zip
wget -O app.zip https://example.com/file.zip
wget -c https://example.com/file.zip
```

### C. Listening ports and connections

```bash
ss -tuln
sudo ss -tulpn
ss -tulpn | grep 3000
netstat -tuln
```

Key flags:
- `-t` — TCP.
- `-u` — UDP.
- `-l` — listening sockets.
- `-n` — numeric addresses and ports.
- `-p` — process information, when permitted.

`ss` is generally preferred over the older `netstat` utility.

### D. DNS troubleshooting

```bash
nslookup google.com
nslookup google.com 8.8.8.8

dig google.com
dig +short google.com
dig google.com A
dig google.com AAAA
dig google.com MX
dig google.com NS
dig www.example.com CNAME
```

DNS record types:
- `A` — IPv4 address.
- `AAAA` — IPv6 address.
- `MX` — mail server.
- `NS` — authoritative name server.
- `CNAME` — alias to another domain name.

### E. Network path

```bash
